        <fig id="article-31255.image.f2" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Guyon Canal Zones. This illustration shows the zones of ulnar nerve compression in the Guyon canal. Zone 1&#x000a0;represents&#x000a0;the area proximal to the ulnar nerve bifurcation into sensory and motor branches. Zone 2 encompasses&#x000a0;the area of the&#x000a0;deep motor branch of the ulnar nerve. Zone 3&#x000a0;represents the area&#x000a0;of&#x000a0;the&#x000a0;superficial sensory branch. Image courtesy S Bhimji MD</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="guyoncanal" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
      <floats-group id="article-31255.s14">
        <fig id="article-31255.image.f3" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Forearm&#x000a0;Artery Dissection. This image displays an anatomical dissection of the forearm, highlighting the radial artery at point A, the course of the median nerve, and the surrounding flexor muscles. The pointers&#x000a0;in other locations, from proximal to distal,&#x000a0;indicate the brachial, ulnar, and&#x000a0;superficial palmar arteries. Image courtesy S Bhimji MD</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="radial-artery-location-arteries-of-the-upper-limb-teachmeanatomy" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
